<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>continuum_arm_soft</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version='1.9'>model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
   <name>Aabhash Bhandari</name>
  </author>

  <description>
    3-tendon soft continuum robotic arm mounted on a cylindrical adapter
    base (radius 0.04m, height 0.02m). The 0.30m arm is discretized into
    15 rigid cylindrical segments (0.02m each), connected by 2-DOF
    universal joints (X/Y bending). Passive silicone compliance is modeled
    with native gz-sim joint spring dynamics (K_theta=1.25 N*m/rad,
    damping=0.08) on every joint axis. Segments are shaded in a navy-to-
    cyan blue gradient (base to tip) purely for visual identification of
    the arm in a composed scene.

    Actuated by the TendonArmController model plugin (see
    plugins/tendon_arm_controller), which subscribes to a 3-tendon length
    command (gz.msgs.Vector3d on /continuum_arm_soft/tendon_cmd, x=l1,
    y=l2, z=l3, tendons spaced 120deg apart at pitch radius d=0.018m),
    maps it to constant-curvature target bend angles (theta_x, theta_y) via
    the standard 3-tendon Jacobian, distributes theta_x/N and theta_y/N as
    the per-joint target, and drives every joint toward that target with a
    PD force loop layered on top of the passive spring dynamics.

    Joint state (actual, physics-integrated angles) is published via the
    stock JointStatePublisher system on /continuum_arm_soft/joint_states.

    Mount contract: continuum_arm_soft/base_cyl's top face (z=0 in this
    module's own frame) is the attachment interface, meant for a
    bottom-mounted glue joint from a composing vehicle model (e.g.
    hillstar), the same pattern rigid_arm_3link uses - see that model's
    header comment for the reasoning.
  </description>
</model>
